    {
      "url": "https://unmark.grandimam.com/",
      "title": "Show HN: Stop applying to jobs using AI-generated resume",
      "source": "hackernews",
      "sourceName": "Hacker News",
      "summary": "When LLMs hands you a resume or pdf it carry markers of how it was made, including the source. You can&#x27;t see them on the page but applicant tracking systems can read it.<p>So recruiters are flagging such profiles and rejecting them entirely. I had tested this across 40+ AI models (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Meta, etc) to produce a resume and every single file carried a marker.<p>To solve this problem. I had built a free tool to show what your file says and gives you a cleaned version:<p>- Drop your resume and get a cleaned copy\n- Free, no account.<p>What it doesn&#x27;t do: it won&#x27;t rewrite your resume or make AI-sounding wording more human. It only deals with what&#x27;s hidden in the file.<p>It&#x27;s a simple tool, but it feels absolutely necessary now as more people are using AI for generating their entire resume or even editing them. I am the developer, happy to answer any questions.",
