    {
      "url": "https://github.com/Musset-App/musset",
      "title": "Show HN: Musset, open-source Scrivener alternative with an AI that never writes",
      "source": "hackernews",
      "sourceName": "Hacker News",
      "summary": "I’m writing my first novel and could not find an app that fit my workflow: quiet like iA Writer, organized like Scrivener, and with AI so I can discuss my book while I write it. It allows me to feel less “alone” and have a sounding board while I write.<p>- A book is a folder of plain Markdown files. Musset commits to a git repo, tracks versions and drafts without you having to know git.<p>- Revisions are CriticMarkup inside the text. It manages docx revisions too, so your editor can edit a Word doc and you import their comments.<p>- PDFs are typeset using Typst, embedded in the app, following each language’s typographic rules.<p>- Spelling and grammar are checked using LanguageTool, also embedded.<p>- Mac&#x2F;Word, WordStar, vi and Emacs keyboard modes.<p>The AI is optional and uses your Codex or Claude Code CLI. It comments, leaves margin notes, and checks continuity and your chapters against your style rules.<p>It’s GPL-3.0 and free during the beta. When or if it reaches 1.0, if there is sufficient interest, the idea is to make it a small one-time payment ($9.90). There is a paid sync service (git hosting) that lets you share a book with beta readers and editors.<p>Download: <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;musset.app\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;musset.app</a><p>I’d love to have some feedback!",
      "author": "julienmarie",
